      "title": "About Mountaineering Incident",
      "subject": "Mountaineering Incident",
      "summary": "This event concerns an avalanche that struck a 10-person climbing expedition on Broad Peak in Pakistan’s Karakoram range on July 30, 2026. The expedition included high-altitude climber Nirmal Purja; by August 1, the expedition company said all 10 climbers had died while recovery efforts continued.",
      "facts": [
        {
          "label": "Incident date and reported toll",
          "value": "The avalanche occurred on July 30, 2026. On August 1, Elite Exped, the expedition company, said that Purja and the other nine climbers in the group had died.",
          "source_ids": [
            "o1",
            "o2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "Location",
          "value": "Broad Peak is an approximately 8,051-meter mountain in the Karakoram, on the Pakistan-China border and near K2; it is among the world’s fourteen mountains above 8,000 meters.",
          "source_ids": [
            "o3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "Expedition",
          "value": "The affected party was a 10-member expedition led by Nepal-born mountaineer Nirmal Purja, also known as Nims Dai; Pakistani rescuers began searching in severe conditions after the avalanche.",
          "source_ids": [
            "o2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "Mountaineering oversight",
          "value": "Climbing and trekking activity in Gilgit-Baltistan is regulated by the regional tourism authorities: expeditions require registration and permits in restricted areas, and the government states that the Department of Tourism is the authority issuing climbing permits.",
          "source_ids": [
            "o4",
            "o5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "Permit category",
          "value": "Pakistan’s Gilgit-Baltistan tourism rules place peaks from 8,001 to 8,500 meters in a permit-and-royalty category; Broad Peak falls within that elevation band.",
          "source_ids": [
            "o6",
            "o7"
